{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-df70b2510c5c", "start_time": "2026-09-21T20:59:49.517Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-21T21:00:00.896Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 13679, "tokens_out": 282, "latency": 4.7455, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "Give me a status summary of claim TM-2026-0061 and list the next steps.", "prompt_hash": "sha256:6f7aa5221d2ac2afa35990da81be49570703413979222a333ea877dcc5bfdd6a", "response_text": "## Status summary: TM-2026-0061\n\n**Policyholder:** Halstead Joinery Limited  \n**Policy:** TM-CP-118460 (Commercial property, fire)  \n**Incident:** Fire in dust extraction plant, 2 April 2026  \n**Cause:** Failed bearing  \n**Status:** Open\n\n**Financial position:**\n- Reserve: £214,000\n- Paid to date: £60,000\n- Outstanding: £154,000\n\n**Key points:**\n- Large loss, escalated to Large Loss Unit on notification day\n- Hot work permit records have been obtained and reviewed\n- Business interruption claim running concurrently with twelve-month indemnity period\n- Reinsurance team notified 3 April 2026\n\n**Next steps:**\n\nTo give you accurate next steps, I need to check the case file for the most recent handler notes. Let me do that now.", "response_hash": "sha256:bddbd5072ae9441ad02b83246c2532a3705cee4601081e8ea7e403200a797ff8", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-df70b2510c5c", "start_time": "2026-09-21T20:59:49.517Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 2, "timestamp": "2026-09-21T21:00:01.161Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 14498, "tokens_out": 308, "latency": 0.2643, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "Give me a status summary of claim TM-2026-0061 and list the next steps.", "prompt_hash": "sha256:6f7aa5221d2ac2afa35990da81be49570703413979222a333ea877dcc5bfdd6a", "response_text": "## Revised status summary and next steps: TM-2026-0061\n\n**Current position (as at 2 June 2026):**\n\nThe claim is progressing through investigation and reserve assessment. Material damage and business interruption elements are both being handled in parallel.\n\n**Next steps:**\n\n1. **Recovery action** – Referred to recovery team on 2 June 2026 for pursuit against the maintenance contractor. Service records show inspection interval breached (last inspection eleven months before fire, contractual interval six months). This is the most time-sensitive item.\n\n2. **Business interruption quantification** – Forensic accountant continuing review of the twelve-month indemnity period. The insured's mitigation through subcontractor use has been authorised as increased cost of working and reduces the loss exposure.\n\n3. **Material damage finalisation** – £60,000 interim payment released in April; remaining £100,000 material damage (plus fees) to be settled once adjuster confirms reinstatement costs for the extraction plant and adjoining finishing shop/roof.\n\n4. **Reinsurance management** – Keep reinsurance team updated as recovery and business interruption elements develop, given the loss exceeds 50% of property retention.\n\nI'd recommend checking with the recovery team on progress of the maintenance contractor claim, and getting an update from the forensic accountant on the business interruption conclusion.", "response_hash": "sha256:dbbc311daf29832f3fa773ca58cf844bb7b739a92bc59fb979b9e0a49923aaa4", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
